      :createdAt 1789171200000
      :updatedAt 1789418200000
      :motivation "Home, docs and blog repeatedly use max-w-6xl, but data surfaces need more room while narrative copy should not become a full-width wall of text."
      :purpose "Add shared shell conventions: 72rem primary frame, max 68ch reading measure that shrinks with the viewport, 80rem opt-in data canvas, CSS grid for split layouts, safe-area padding and overflow containment."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Shared shell classes" "No horizontal overflow at 320, 768, 1024 and 1440 CSS pixels" "Data surfaces can widen without widening prose" "Explicit breakout/grid keeps 80rem data surfaces outside the prose flow" "Hero and docs remain readable"]
      :owns ["asl/web/src/App.asl" "asl/web/src/views/HomeView.asl" "asl/web/src/views/DocsView.asl" "asl/web/src/views/BlogView.asl" "asl/web/src/views/RoadmapView.asl" "asl/web/src/components/SkyLoomVisualizer.asl" "asl/web/src/components/ModuleGraphVisualizer.asl" "asl/web/src/components/InBrowserAgent.asl" "asl/web/src/components/InBrowserCompanion.asl" "asl/web/src/components/UnifiedPackageMatrix.asl"]
